      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "BlogPosting",
        "headline": "TV Has Sound but No Picture: Causes and Fixes",
        "description": "Why a TV plays sound with a black screen, the one-minute torch test that tells you the cause, and what each fix typically costs in Delhi NCR.",
        "image": "https://grsolution.co.in/images/blog/tv-sound-but-no-picture.webp",
        "url": "https://grsolution.co.in/blog/tv-sound-but-no-picture",
        "datePublished": "2026-09-25",
        "dateModified": "2026-09-25",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GR Solution Editorial Team",
          "url": "https://grsolution.co.in/about"
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@id": "https://grsolution.co.in/#organization"
        },
        "mainEntityOfPage": {
          "@type": "WebPage",
          "@id": "https://grsolution.co.in/blog/tv-sound-but-no-picture"
        },
        "inLanguage": "en-IN",
        "isPartOf": {
          "@id": "https://grsolution.co.in/#website"
        }
      },
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Why does my TV have sound but no picture?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Usually because the backlight has failed. The panel is still producing an image, but there is no light behind it. Shine a torch at the screen at a sharp angle: a faint image confirms it."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Can I fix sound but no picture myself?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "You can rule out settings, inputs and a stuck standby state yourself. Replacing backlight strips means separating the panel, which is easy to crack, so that part is best left to a technician."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How much does it cost to fix a TV with no picture?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "In the Delhi NCR market, backlight replacement runs roughly ₹3,000–₹8,000 on 32”–43” sets and ₹5,500–₹12,000 on 44”–55” sets. A T-Con fault is often cheaper. Panel replacement is the expensive exception."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
